# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Definition of purifications {#definition-of-purifications}"
msgstr "Definição de purificações {#definition-of-purifications}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us begin with a precise mathematical definition for purifications.\n"
msgstr "Vamos começar com uma definição matemática precisa para purificações.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Definition\">\n"
"Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system in a state represented by a density matrix $\\rho$, and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a quantum state vector of a pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that leaves $\\rho$ when $\\mathsf{Y}$ is traced out:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
"The state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is then said to be a *purification* of $\\rho$.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Definição\">\n"
"Suponha que $\\mathsf{X}$ é um sistema em um estado representado por uma matriz de densidade $\\rho$, e $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ é um vetor de estado quântico do par $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ que resulta em $\\rho$ quando $\\mathsf{Y}$ é traçado fora:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
"O vetor de estado $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ é então dito ser uma *purificação* de $\\rho$.\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pure state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$, expressed as a density matrix rather than a quantum state vector, is also commonly referred to as a purification of $\\rho$ when the equation in the definition is true, but we'll generally use the term to refer to a quantum state vector.\n"
msgstr "O estado puro $\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$, expresso como uma matriz de densidade em vez de um vetor de estado quântico, também é comumente referido como uma purificação de $\\rho$ quando a equação na definição é verdadeira, mas geralmente usaremos o termo para se referir a um vetor de estado quântico.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The term *purification* is also used more generally when the ordering of the systems is reversed, when the names of the systems and states are different (of course), and when there are more than two systems.\n"
"For instance, if $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ is a quantum state vector representing a pure state of a compound system $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C})$, and the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"O termo *purificação* também é usado de forma mais geral quando a ordem dos sistemas é invertida, quando os nomes dos sistemas e estados são diferentes (é claro), e quando há mais de dois sistemas.\n"
"Por exemplo, se $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ é um vetor de estado quântico representando um estado puro de um sistema composto $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C})$, e a equação\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is true for a density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of the system $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{C})$, then $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is still referred to as a purification of $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr "é verdadeira para uma matriz de densidade $\\rho$ representando um estado do sistema $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{C})$, então $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ainda é referido como uma purificação de $\\rho$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the purposes of this lesson, however, we'll focus on the specific form described in the definition.\n"
"Properties and facts concerning purifications, according to this definition, can typically be generalized to more than two systems by re-ordering and partitioning the systems into two compound systems, one playing the role of $\\mathsf{X}$ and the other playing the role of $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para os fins desta lição, no entanto, vamos nos concentrar na forma específica descrita na definição.\n"
"Propriedades e fatos sobre purificações, de acordo com essa definição, podem ser generalizados para mais de dois sistemas reorganizando e particionando os sistemas em dois sistemas compostos, um desempenhando o papel de $\\mathsf{X}$ e o outro desempenhando o papel de $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Existence of purifications {#existence-of-purifications}"
msgstr "Existência de purificações {#existence-of-purifications}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are any two systems and $\\rho$ is a given state of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"We will prove that there exists a quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that *purifies* $\\rho$ — which is another way of saying that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a purification of $\\rho$ — provided that the system $\\mathsf{Y}$ is large enough.\n"
"In particular, if $\\mathsf{Y}$ has at least as many classical states as $\\mathsf{X}$, then a purification of this form necessarily exists for every state $\\rho$.\n"
"Fewer classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ are required for some states $\\rho;$\n"
"in general, $\\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ are necessary and sufficient for the existence of a quantum state vector of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that purifies $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Suponha que $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ são quaisquer dois sistemas e $\\rho$ é um estado dado de $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Vamos provar que existe um vetor de estado quântico $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ de $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ que *purifica* $\\rho$ — o que é outra forma de dizer que $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ é uma purificação de $\\rho$ — desde que o sistema $\\mathsf{Y}$ seja grande o suficiente.\n"
"Em particular, se $\\mathsf{Y}$ tem pelo menos tantos estados clássicos quanto $\\mathsf{X},$ então uma purificação dessa forma necessariamente existe para todo estado $\\rho.$\n"
"Menos estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{Y}$ são necessários para alguns estados $\\rho;$\n"
"em geral, $\\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{Y}$ são necessários e suficientes para a existência de um vetor de estado quântico de $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ que purifica $\\rho.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider first any expression of $\\rho$ as a convex combination of $n$ pure states, for any positive integer $n$.\n"
msgstr "Considere primeiro qualquer expressão de $\\rho$ como uma combinação convexa de $n$ estados puros, para qualquer inteiro positivo $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this expression, $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ is a probability vector and $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ are quantum state vectors of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr "Nessa expressão, $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ é um vetor de probabilidade e $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ são vetores de estado quântico de $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One way to obtain such an expression is through the spectral theorem, in which case $n$ is the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$, $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ are the eigenvalues of $\\rho$, and $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ are orthonormal eigenvectors corresponding to these eigenvalues.\n"
msgstr "Uma forma de obter essa expressão é pelo teorema espectral, em que $n$ é o número de estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{X},$ $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ são os autovalores de $\\rho,$ e $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ são autovetores ortonormais correspondentes a esses autovalores.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's actually no need to include the terms corresponding to the zero eigenvalues of $\\rho$ in the sum, which allows us to alternatively choose $n = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ and $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ to be the non-zero eigenvalues of $\\rho$.\n"
"This is the minimum value of $n$ for which an expression of $\\rho$ taking the form above exists.\n"
msgstr ""
"Na verdade, não é necessário incluir na soma os termos correspondentes aos autovalores zero de $\\rho$, o que nos permite alternativamente escolher $n = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ e $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ como os autovalores não nulos de $\\rho$.\n"
"Esse é o valor mínimo de $n$ para o qual uma expressão de $\\rho$ na forma acima existe.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, it is *not necessary* that the chosen expression of $\\rho$, as a convex combination of pure states, comes from the spectral theorem — this is just one way to obtain such an expression.\n"
"In particular, $n$ could be any positive integer, the unit vectors $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ need not be orthogonal, and the probabilities $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ need not be eigenvalues of $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ficar claro, *não é necessário* que a expressão escolhida de $\\rho,$ como uma combinação convexa de estados puros, venha do teorema espectral — essa é apenas uma maneira de obter tal expressão.\n"
"Em particular, $n$ pode ser qualquer inteiro positivo, os vetores unitários $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ não precisam ser ortogonais, e as probabilidades $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ não precisam ser autovalores de $\\rho.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now identify a purification of $\\rho$ as follows.\n"
msgstr "Podemos agora identificar uma purificação de $\\rho$ da seguinte forma.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're making the assumption that the classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ include $0,\\ldots,n-1$.\n"
"If they do not, an arbitrary choice for $n$ distinct classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ can be substituted for $0,\\ldots,n-1$.\n"
"Verifying that this is indeed a purification of $\\rho$ is a simple matter of computing the partial trace, which can be done in the following two equivalent ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui estamos assumindo que os estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{Y}$ incluem $0,\\ldots,n-1$.\n"
"Se não incluírem, uma escolha arbitrária de $n$ estados clássicos distintos de $\\mathsf{Y}$ pode ser substituída por $0,\\ldots,n-1$.\n"
"Verificar que isso é de fato uma purificação de $\\rho$ é uma simples questão de calcular o traço parcial, o que pode ser feito das duas seguintes maneiras equivalentes.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\langle a\\vert) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\langle a\\vert) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_b\\vert\n"
"\\, \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert a \\rangle \\langle b \\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_b\\vert\n"
"\\, \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert a \\rangle \\langle b \\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More generally, for any orthonormal set of vectors $\\{\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$, the quantum state vector\n"
msgstr "De forma mais geral, para qualquer conjunto ortonormal de vetores $\\{\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$, o vetor de estado quântico\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is a purification of $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr "is a purification of $\\rho$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example {#example}"
msgstr "Exemplo {#example}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are both qubits and\n"
msgstr "Suponha que $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ são ambos qubits e\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is a density matrix representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr "é uma matriz de densidade representando um estado de $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can use the spectral theorem to express $\\rho$ as\n"
msgstr "Podemos usar o teorema espectral para expressar $\\rho$ como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle = \\cos(\\theta) \\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta)\\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
"The quantum state vector\n"
msgstr ""
"onde $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle = \\cos(\\theta) \\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta)\\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
"O vetor de estado quântico\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\sin(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\sin(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which describes a pure state of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$, is therefore a purification of $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr "que descreve um estado puro do par $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$, é portanto uma purificação de $\\rho$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, we can write\n"
msgstr "Alternativamente, podemos escrever\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a convex combination of pure states but not a spectral decomposition because $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert +\\rangle$ are not orthogonal and $1/2$ is not an eigenvalue of $\\rho$.\n"
"Nevertheless, the quantum state vector\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta é uma combinação convexa de estados puros, mas não uma decomposição espectral porque $\\vert 0\\rangle$ e $\\vert +\\rangle$ não são ortogonais e $1/2$ não é um autovalor de $\\rho$.\n"
"Ainda assim, o vetor de estado quântico\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Schmidt decompositions {#schmidt-decompositions}"
msgstr "Decomposições de Schmidt {#schmidt-decompositions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we will discuss *Schmidt decompositions*, which are expressions of quantum state vectors of *pairs* of systems that take a certain form.\n"
"Schmidt decompositions are closely connected with purifications, and they're very useful in their own right.\n"
"Indeed, when reasoning about a given quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ of a pair of systems, the first step is often to identify or consider a Schmidt decomposition of this state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, vamos discutir as *decomposições de Schmidt*, que são expressões de vetores de estado quântico de *pares* de sistemas que assumem uma determinada forma.\n"
"As decomposições de Schmidt estão intimamente ligadas às purificações e são muito úteis por si mesmas.\n"
"De fato, ao raciocinar sobre um dado vetor de estado quântico $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ de um par de sistemas, o primeiro passo costuma ser identificar ou considerar uma decomposição de Schmidt desse estado.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Definition\">\n"
"Let $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ be a given quantum state vector of a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$. A *Schmidt decomposition* of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an expression of the form\n"
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
"where $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ are positive real numbers summing to $1$ and *both* of the sets $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ and $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are orthonormal.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Definição\">\n"
"Seja $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ um dado vetor de estado quântico de um par de sistemas $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$. Uma *decomposição de Schmidt* de $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ é uma expressão da forma\n"
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
"onde $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ são números reais positivos que somam $1$ e *ambos* os conjuntos $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ e $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ são ortonormais.\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The values\n"
msgstr "Os valores\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{p_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{p_{r-1}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{p_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{p_{r-1}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"in a Schmidt decomposition of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ are known as its *Schmidt coefficients*, which are uniquely determined (up to their ordering) — they're the only positive real numbers that can appear in such an expression of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"The sets\n"
msgstr ""
"em uma decomposição de Schmidt de $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ são conhecidos como seus *coeficientes de Schmidt*, que são unicamente determinados (a menos de sua ordenação) — são os únicos números reais positivos que podem aparecer em tal expressão de $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"Os conjuntos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\} \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\} \\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "on the other hand, are not uniquely determined, and the freedom one has in choosing these sets of vectors will be clarified in the explanation that follows.\n"
msgstr "por outro lado, não são unicamente determinados, e a liberdade que se tem na escolha desses conjuntos de vetores ficará clara na explicação que se segue.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll now verify that a given quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ does indeed have a Schmidt decomposition, and in the process, we'll learn how to find one.\n"
msgstr "Vamos agora verificar que um dado vetor de estado quântico $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ de fato possui uma decomposição de Schmidt e, no processo, aprenderemos como encontrá-la.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider first an arbitrary (not necessarily orthogonal) basis $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ of the vector space corresponding to the system $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Because this is a basis, there will always exist a uniquely determined selection of vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ for which the following equation is true.\n"
msgstr ""
"Considere primeiro uma base arbitrária (não necessariamente ortogonal) $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ do espaço vetorial correspondente ao sistema $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Como essa é uma base, sempre existirá uma seleção unicamente determinada de vetores $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ para os quais a equação a seguir é verdadeira.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a \\rangle\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a \\rangle\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, suppose $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is the standard basis associated with $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Assuming the classical state set of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, this means that $\\vert x_a\\rangle = \\vert a\\rangle$ for each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, and we find that\n"
msgstr ""
"Por exemplo, suponha que $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ seja a base padrão associada a $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Assumindo que o conjunto de estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{X}$ é $\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, isso significa que $\\vert x_a\\rangle = \\vert a\\rangle$ para cada $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, e encontramos que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "when\n"
msgstr "quando\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = ( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = ( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$.\n"
"We frequently consider expressions like this when contemplating a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"para cada $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$.\n"
"Frequentemente consideramos expressões como essa ao contemplar uma medição na base padrão de $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It's important to note that the formula\n"
msgstr "É importante notar que a fórmula\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for the vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ in this example only works because $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert n-1\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal* basis.\n"
"In general, if $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is a basis that is not necessarily orthonormal, then the vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ are still uniquely determined by the equation $(1)$, but a different formula is needed.\n"
"One way to find them is first to identify vectors $\\vert w_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert w_{n-1}\\rangle$ so that the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"para os vetores $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ neste exemplo só funciona porque $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert n-1\\rangle\\}$ é uma base *ortonormal*.\n"
"Em geral, se $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ é uma base não necessariamente ortonormal, então os vetores $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ ainda são unicamente determinados pela equação $(1)$, mas uma fórmula diferente é necessária.\n"
"Uma maneira de encontrá-los é primeiro identificar vetores $\\vert w_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert w_{n-1}\\rangle$ tais que a equação\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle w_a \\vert x_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases} 1 & a=b\\\\ 0 & a\\neq b \\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle w_a \\vert x_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases} 1 & a=b\\\\ 0 & a\\neq b \\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is satisfied for all $a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, at which point we have\n"
msgstr "seja satisfeita para todos $a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, momento em que temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = (\\langle w_a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = (\\langle w_a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a given basis $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ of the vector space corresponding to $\\mathsf{X}$, the uniquely determined vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ for which the equation $(1)$ is satisfied won't necessarily satisfy any special properties, even if $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ happens to be an orthonormal basis.\n"
"If, however, we choose $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ to be an orthonormal basis of *eigenvectors* of the reduced state\n"
msgstr ""
"Para uma dada base $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ do espaço vetorial correspondente a $\\mathsf{X}$, os vetores unicamente determinados $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ para os quais a equação $(1)$ é satisfeita não necessariamente satisfazem propriedades especiais, mesmo que $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ seja uma base ortonormal.\n"
"Se, no entanto, escolhermos $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ como uma base ortonormal de *autovetores* do estado reduzido\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr),\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"then something interesting happens.\n"
"Specifically, for the uniquely determined collection $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ for which the equation $(1)$ is true, we find that this collection must be *orthogonal.*\n"
msgstr ""
"algo interessante acontece.\n"
"Especificamente, para a coleção unicamente determinada $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ para a qual a equação $(1)$ é verdadeira, descobrimos que essa coleção deve ser *ortogonal.*\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In greater detail, consider a spectral decomposition of $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr "Em mais detalhes, considere uma decomposição espectral de $\\rho$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're denoting the eigenvalues of $\\rho$ by $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ in recognition of the fact that $\\rho$ is a density matrix — so the vector of eigenvalues $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ forms a probability vector — while $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of eigenvectors corresponding to these eigenvalues.\n"
"To see that the unique collection $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ for which the equation $(1)$ is true is necessarily orthogonal, we can begin by computing the partial trace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui estamos denotando os autovalores de $\\rho$ por $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ em reconhecimento ao fato de que $\\rho$ é uma matriz densidade — portanto o vetor de autovalores $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ forma um vetor de probabilidade — enquanto $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ é uma base ortonormal de autovetores correspondentes a esses autovalores.\n"
"Para ver que a coleção única $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ para a qual a equação $(1)$ é verdadeira é necessariamente ortogonal, podemos começar calculando o traço parcial.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert z_a\\rangle\\langle z_b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\langle z_b\\vert z_a\\rangle \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert z_a\\rangle\\langle z_b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\langle z_b\\vert z_a\\rangle \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This expression must agree with the spectral decomposition of $\\rho$.\n"
"Because $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is a basis, we conclude that the set of matrices\n"
msgstr ""
"Essa expressão deve concordar com a decomposição espectral de $\\rho$.\n"
"Como $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ é uma base, concluímos que o conjunto de matrizes\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\,:\\, a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\} \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\,:\\, a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\} \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is linearly independent, and so it follows that\n"
msgstr "é linearmente independente, e portanto segue que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle z_b \\vert z_a\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  p_a & a=b\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  0 & a\\neq b,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle z_b \\vert z_a\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  p_a & a=b\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  0 & a\\neq b,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "establishing that $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is orthogonal.\n"
msgstr "estabelecendo que $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ é ortogonal.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've nearly obtained a Schmidt decomposition of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"It remains to discard those terms in $(1)$ for which $p_a = 0$ and then write $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ for a unit vector $\\vert y_a\\rangle$ for each of the remaining terms.\n"
msgstr ""
"Estamos quase obtendo uma decomposição de Schmidt de $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"Resta descartar os termos em $(1)$ para os quais $p_a = 0$ e então escrever $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ para um vetor unitário $\\vert y_a\\rangle$ para cada um dos termos restantes.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A convenient way to do this begins with the observation that we're free to number the eigenvalue/eigenvector pairs in a spectral decomposition of the reduced state $\\rho$ however we wish — so we may assume that the eigenvalues are sorted in decreasing order:\n"
msgstr "Uma maneira conveniente de fazer isso começa com a observação de que somos livres para numerar os pares autovalor/autovetor em uma decomposição espectral do estado reduzido $\\rho$ como quisermos — então podemos assumir que os autovalores estão ordenados em ordem decrescente:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p_0 \\geq p_1 \\geq \\cdots \\geq p_{n-1}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p_0 \\geq p_1 \\geq \\cdots \\geq p_{n-1}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Letting $r = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$, we find that $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1} > 0$ and $p_r = \\cdots = p_{n-1} = 0$.\n"
"So, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Seja $r = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$, encontramos que $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1} > 0$ e $p_r = \\cdots = p_{n-1} = 0$.\n"
"Portanto, temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and we can write the quantum state vector $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ as\n"
msgstr "e podemos escrever o vetor de estado quântico $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given that\n"
msgstr "Dado que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\| \\vert z_a \\rangle \\|^2 = \\langle z_a \\vert z_a \\rangle = p_a > 0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\| \\vert z_a \\rangle \\|^2 = \\langle z_a \\vert z_a \\rangle = p_a > 0\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for $a=0,\\ldots,r-1$, we can define unit vectors $\\vert y_0 \\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle$ as\n"
msgstr "para $a=0,\\ldots,r-1$, podemos definir vetores unitários $\\vert y_0 \\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle$ como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert y_a\\rangle = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\|\\vert z_a\\rangle\\|} = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\sqrt{p_a}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert y_a\\rangle = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\|\\vert z_a\\rangle\\|} = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\sqrt{p_a}},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"so that $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ for each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,r-1\\}$.\n"
"Because the vectors $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert z_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are orthogonal and nonzero, it follows that\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal* set, and so we have obtained a Schmidt decomposition of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"de modo que $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ para cada $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,r-1\\}$.\n"
"Como os vetores $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert z_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ são ortogonais e não nulos, segue que\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ é um conjunto *ortonormal*, e assim obtivemos uma decomposição de Schmidt de $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Concerning the choice of the vectors\n"
"$\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$,\n"
"we can select $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ to be any orthonormal set of eigenvectors corresponding to the nonzero eigenvalues of the reduced state $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ (as we have done above), in which case the vectors $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are uniquely determined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Com relação à escolha dos vetores\n"
"$\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ e\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$,\n"
"podemos selecionar $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ como qualquer conjunto ortonormal de autovetores correspondentes aos autovalores não nulos do estado reduzido $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ (como fizemos acima), caso em que os vetores $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ ficam unicamente determinados.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The situation is symmetric between the two systems, so we can alternatively choose $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ to be any orthonormal set of eigenvectors corresponding to the nonzero eigenvalues of the reduced state $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$, in which case the vectors $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ will be uniquely determined.\n"
msgstr "A situação é simétrica entre os dois sistemas, então podemos alternativamente escolher $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ como qualquer conjunto ortonormal de autovetores correspondentes aos autovalores não nulos do estado reduzido $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$, caso em que os vetores $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ ficarão unicamente determinados.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notice, however, that once one of the sets is selected, as a set of eigenvectors of the corresponding reduced state as just described, the other is determined — so they cannot be chosen independently.\n"
msgstr "Note, no entanto, que uma vez que um dos conjuntos é selecionado como conjunto de autovetores do estado reduzido correspondente como descrito acima, o outro fica determinado — portanto eles não podem ser escolhidos de forma independente.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Although it won't come up again in this series, it is noteworthy that the non-zero eigenvalues $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ of the reduced state $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ must always agree with the nonzero eigenvalues of the reduced state $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ for any pure state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ of a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
msgstr "Embora não apareça novamente nesta série, é notável que os autovalores não nulos $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ do estado reduzido $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ devem sempre concordar com os autovalores não nulos do estado reduzido $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ para qualquer estado puro $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ de um par de sistemas $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, the reduced states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ have exactly the same amount of randomness in them when the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is in a pure state.\n"
"This fact is revealed by the Schmidt decomposition: in both cases the eigenvalues of the reduced states must agree with the squares of the Schmidt coefficients of the pure state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Falando intuitivamente, os estados reduzidos de $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ possuem exatamente a mesma quantidade de aleatoriedade quando o par $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ está em um estado puro.\n"
"Esse fato é revelado pela decomposição de Schmidt: em ambos os casos, os autovalores dos estados reduzidos devem concordar com os quadrados dos coeficientes de Schmidt do estado puro.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unitary equivalence of purifications {#unitary-equivalence-of-purifications}"
msgstr "Equivalência unitária de purificações {#unitary-equivalence-of-purifications}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can use Schmidt decompositions to establish a fundamentally important fact concerning purifications known as the *unitary equivalence of purifications*.\n"
msgstr "Podemos usar decomposições de Schmidt para estabelecer um fato fundamentalmente importante sobre purificações, conhecido como a *equivalência unitária de purificações*.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Unitary equivalence of purifications: Suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are systems, and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ are quantum state vectors of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that both purify the same state of $\\mathsf{X}$. In symbols,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"
"for some density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"There must then exist a unitary operation $U$ on $\\mathsf{Y}$ alone that transforms the first purification into the second:\n"
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert\\phi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Teorema\">\n"
"Equivalência unitária de purificações: Suponha que $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ são sistemas, e $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ e $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ são vetores de estado quântico de $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ que purificam o mesmo estado de $\\mathsf{X}$. Em símbolos,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"
"para alguma matriz densidade $\\rho$ representando um estado de $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Deve então existir uma operação unitária $U$ em $\\mathsf{Y}$ sozinho que transforma a primeira purificação na segunda:\n"
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert\\phi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll discuss a few implications of this theorem as the lesson continues, but first let's see how it follows from our previous discussion of Schmidt decompositions.\n"
msgstr "Vamos discutir algumas implicações desse teorema ao longo da lição, mas primeiro vamos ver como ele decorre da nossa discussão anterior sobre decomposições de Schmidt.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our assumption is that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ are quantum state vectors\n"
"of a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that satisfy the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"Nossa hipótese é que $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ e $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ são vetores de estado quântico\n"
"de um par de sistemas $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ que satisfazem a equação\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for some density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr "para alguma matriz densidade $\\rho$ representando um estado de $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider a spectral decomposition of $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr "Considere uma decomposição espectral de $\\rho$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of eigenvectors of $\\rho$.\n"
"By following the prescription described previously we can obtain Schmidt decompositions for both $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ having the following form.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ é uma base ortonormal de autovetores de $\\rho$.\n"
"Seguindo a prescrição descrita anteriormente, podemos obter decomposições de Schmidt para $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ e $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ com a seguinte forma.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\phi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\phi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In these expressions $r$ is the rank of $\\rho$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are orthonormal sets of vectors in the space corresponding to $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nessas expressões$,r$ é o posto de $\\rho$ e\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ e\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ são conjuntos ortonormais de vetores no espaço correspondente a $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For any two orthonormal sets in the same space that have the same number of elements, there's always a unitary matrix that transforms the first set into the second, so we can choose a unitary matrix $U$ so that $U \\vert u_a\\rangle = \\vert v_a\\rangle$ for $a = 0,\\ldots,r-1$.\n"
"In particular, to find such a matrix $U$ we can first use the Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process to extend our orthonormal sets to orthonormal bases\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{m-1}\\rangle\\}$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{m-1}\\rangle\\}$, where $m$ is the dimension of the space corresponding to $\\mathsf{Y}$, and then take\n"
msgstr ""
"Para quaisquer dois conjuntos ortonormais no mesmo espaço que têm o mesmo número de elementos, sempre existe uma matriz unitária que transforma o primeiro conjunto no segundo, portanto podemos escolher uma matriz unitária $U$ de modo que $U \\vert u_a\\rangle = \\vert v_a\\rangle$ para $a = 0,\\ldots,r-1$.\n"
"Em particular, para encontrar tal matriz $U$ podemos primeiro usar o processo de ortogonalização de Gram-Schmidt para estender nossos conjuntos ortonormais a bases ortonormais\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{m-1}\\rangle\\}$ e\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{m-1}\\rangle\\}$, onde $m$ é a dimensão do espaço correspondente a $\\mathsf{Y}$, e então tomar\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert v_a\\rangle\\langle u_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert v_a\\rangle\\langle u_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now find that\n"
msgstr "Encontramos agora que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes U \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes U \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which completes the proof.\n"
msgstr "o que completa a prova.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here are just a few of many interesting examples and implications connected with the unitary equivalence of purifications.\n"
"We'll see another critically important one later in the lesson, in the context of fidelity, known as *Uhlmann's theorem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui estão apenas alguns de muitos exemplos e implicações interessantes relacionados à equivalência unitária de purificações.\n"
"Veremos outro de importância crítica mais adiante na lição, no contexto da fidelidade, conhecido como o *teorema de Uhlmann*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding {#superdense-coding}"
msgstr "Codificação superdensa {#superdense-coding}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the superdense coding protocol, Alice and Bob share an e-bit, meaning that Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A}$, Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B}$, and together the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is in the $\\vert\\phi^{+}\\rangle$ Bell state.\n"
"The protocol describes how Alice can transform this shared state into any one of the four Bell states, $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$, $\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle$, $\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle$, and\n"
"$\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle$, by applying a unitary operation to her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
"Once she has done this, she sends $\\mathsf{A}$ to Bob, and then Bob performs a measurement on the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ to see which Bell state he holds.\n"
msgstr ""
"No protocolo de codificação superdensa, Alice e Bob compartilham um e-bit, o que significa que Alice possui um qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob possui um qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ e juntos o par $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ está no estado de Bell $\\vert\\phi^{+}\\rangle.$\n"
"O protocolo descreve como Alice pode transformar esse estado compartilhado em qualquer um dos quatro estados de Bell, $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ $\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle,$ $\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle,$ e\n"
"$\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle,$ aplicando uma operação unitária ao seu qubit $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
"Depois de fazer isso, ela envia $\\mathsf{A}$ para Bob, e então Bob realiza uma medição no par $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ para ver qual estado de Bell ele possui.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For all four Bell states, the reduced state of Bob's qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ is the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr "Para todos os quatro estados de Bell, o estado reduzido do qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ de Bob é o estado completamente misto.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle\\langle\\phi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle\\langle\\phi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle\\langle\\psi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\frac{\\mathbb{I}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle\\langle\\phi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle\\langle\\phi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle\\langle\\psi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\frac{\\mathbb{I}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the unitary equivalence of purifications, we immediately conclude that for each Bell state there must exist a unitary operation on Alice's qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ alone that transforms $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ into the chosen Bell state.\n"
"Although this does not reveal the precise details of the protocol, the unitary equivalence of purifications does immediately imply that superdense coding is possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pela equivalência unitária de purificações, concluímos imediatamente que para cada estado de Bell deve existir uma operação unitária no qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ de Alice sozinho que transforma $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ no estado de Bell escolhido.\n"
"Embora isso não revele os detalhes precisos do protocolo, a equivalência unitária de purificações implica imediatamente que a codificação superdensa é possível.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can also conclude that generalizations of superdense coding to larger systems are always possible, provided that we replace the Bell states with any orthonormal basis of purifications of the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr "Podemos também concluir que generalizações da codificação superdensa para sistemas maiores são sempre possíveis, desde que substituamos os estados de Bell por qualquer base ortonormal de purificações do estado completamente misto.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cryptographic implications {#cryptographic-implications}"
msgstr "Implicações criptográficas {#cryptographic-implications}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The unitary equivalence of purifications has implications concerning the implementation of cryptographic primitives using quantum information.\n"
"For instance, the unitary equivalence of purifications reveals that it is impossible to implement an ideal form of *bit commitment* using quantum information.\n"
msgstr ""
"A equivalência unitária de purificações tem implicações sobre a implementação de primitivas criptográficas usando informação quântica.\n"
"Por exemplo, a equivalência unitária de purificações revela que é impossível implementar uma forma ideal de *bit commitment* usando informação quântica.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bit commitment primitive involves two participants, Alice and Bob (who don't trust one another), and has two phases.\n"
"- The first phase is the *commit* phase, through which Alice commits to a binary value $b\\in\\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"This commitment must be *binding*, which means that Alice cannot change her mind, as well as *concealing*, which means that Bob can't tell which value Alice has committed to.\n"
"- The second phase is the *reveal* phase, in which the bit committed by Alice becomes known to Bob, who should then be convinced that it was truly the committed value that was revealed.\n"
msgstr ""
"A primitiva de bit commitment envolve dois participantes, Alice e Bob (que não confiam um no outro), e tem duas fases.\n"
"- A primeira fase é a fase de *comprometimento*, por meio da qual Alice se compromete com um valor binário $b\\in\\{0,1\\}$.\n"
"Esse comprometimento deve ser *vinculante*, o que significa que Alice não pode mudar de ideia, além de *ocultador*, o que significa que Bob não pode descobrir com qual valor Alice se comprometeu.\n"
"- A segunda fase é a fase de *revelação*, na qual o bit comprometido por Alice se torna conhecido por Bob, que então deve ser convencido de que foi realmente o valor comprometido que foi revelado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In intuitive, operational terms, the first phase of bit commitment should function as if Alice writes a binary value on a piece of paper, locks the paper inside of a safe, and gives the safe to Bob while keeping the key for herself.\n"
"Alice has committed to the binary value written on the paper because the safe is in Bob's possession (so it's binding), but because Bob can't open the safe he can't tell which value Alice committed to (so it's concealing).\n"
"The second phase should work as if Alice hands the key to the safe to Bob, so that he can open the safe to reveal the value to which Alice committed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Em termos intuitivos e operacionais, a primeira fase do bit commitment deve funcionar como se Alice escrevesse um valor binário em um pedaço de papel, trancasse o papel dentro de um cofre e entregasse o cofre para Bob enquanto guarda a chave para si.\n"
"Alice se comprometeu com o valor binário escrito no papel porque o cofre está na posse de Bob (portanto é vinculante), mas como Bob não pode abrir o cofre ele não pode descobrir com qual valor Alice se comprometeu (portanto é ocultador).\n"
"A segunda fase deve funcionar como se Alice entregasse a chave do cofre para Bob, para que ele possa abri-lo e revelar o valor ao qual Alice se comprometeu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As it turns out, it is impossible to implement a perfect bit commitment protocol by means of quantum information alone, for this contradicts the unitary equivalence of purifications.\n"
"Here is a high-level summary of an argument that establishes this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Acontece que é impossível implementar um protocolo perfeito de bit commitment por meio de informação quântica sozinha, pois isso contradiz a equivalência unitária de purificações.\n"
"Aqui está um resumo de alto nível de um argumento que estabelece isso.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To begin, we can assume Alice and Bob only perform unitary operations or introduce new initialized systems as the protocol is executed.\n"
"The fact that every channel has a Stinespring representation allows us to make this assumption.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para começar, podemos assumir que Alice e Bob realizam apenas operações unitárias ou introduzem novos sistemas inicializados à medida que o protocolo é executado.\n"
"O fato de que todo canal possui uma representação de Stinespring nos permite fazer essa suposição.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the end of the commit phase of the protocol, Bob holds in his possession some compound system that must be in one of two quantum states: $\\rho_0$ if Alice committed to the value $0$ and $\\rho_1$ if Alice committed to the value $1$.\n"
"In order for the protocol to be perfectly concealing, Bob should not be able to tell the difference between these two states — so it must be that $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1$.\n"
"(Otherwise there would be a measurement that discriminates these states probabilistically.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Ao final da fase de comprometimento do protocolo, Bob possui em sua posse algum sistema composto que deve estar em um de dois estados quânticos: $\\rho_0$ se Alice se comprometeu com o valor $0$ e $\\rho_1$ se Alice se comprometeu com o valor $1.$\n"
"Para que o protocolo seja perfeitamente ocultador, Bob não deve ser capaz de distinguir esses dois estados — portanto deve ser que $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1.$\n"
"(Caso contrário, haveria uma medição que discrimina esses estados de forma probabilística.)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, because Alice and Bob have only used unitary operations, the state of all of the systems involved in the protocol together after the commit phase must be in a pure state.\n"
"In particular, suppose that $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ is the pure state of all of the systems involved in the protocol when Alice commits to $0$, and $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ is the pure state of all of the systems involved in the protocol when Alice commits to $1$.\n"
"If we write $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ to denote Alice and Bob's (possibly compound) systems, then\n"
msgstr ""
"No entanto, como Alice e Bob usaram apenas operações unitárias, o estado de todos os sistemas envolvidos no protocolo juntos após a fase de comprometimento deve estar em um estado puro.\n"
"Em particular, suponha que $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ seja o estado puro de todos os sistemas envolvidos no protocolo quando Alice se compromete com $0$, e $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ seja o estado puro de todos os sistemas envolvidos no protocolo quando Alice se compromete com $1$.\n"
"Se escrevermos $\\mathsf{A}$ e $\\mathsf{B}$ para denotar os sistemas (possivelmente compostos) de Alice e Bob, então\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_0 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle\\langle\\psi_0\\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\rho_1 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle\\langle\\psi_1\\vert).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_0 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle\\langle\\psi_0\\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\rho_1 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle\\langle\\psi_1\\vert).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given the requirement that $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1$ for a perfectly concealing protocol, we find that $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ are purifications of the same state — and so, by the unitary equivalence of purifications, there must exist a unitary operation $U$ on $\\mathsf{A}$ alone such that\n"
msgstr "Dada a exigência de que $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1$ para um protocolo perfeitamente ocultador, encontramos que $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ e $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ são purificações do mesmo estado — e então, pela equivalência unitária de purificações, deve existir uma operação unitária $U$ em $\\mathsf{A}$ sozinho tal que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(U\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}})\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle = \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(U\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}})\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle = \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice is therefore free to change her commitment from $0$ to $1$ by applying $U$ to $\\mathsf{A}$,\n"
"or from $1$ to $0$ by applying $U^{\\dagger}$, and so the hypothetical protocol being considered completely fails to be binding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice, portanto, pode mudar seu comprometimento de $0$ para $1$ aplicando $U$ a $\\mathsf{A}$,\n"
"ou de $1$ para $0$ aplicando $U^{\\dagger}$, e assim o protocolo hipotético considerado falha completamente em ser vinculante.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters theorem {#hughston-jozsa-wootters-theorem}"
msgstr "Teorema de Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters {#hughston-jozsa-wootters-theorem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last implication of the unitary equivalence of purifications that we'll discuss in this portion of the lesson is the following theorem known as the Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters theorem.\n"
"(This is, in fact, a slightly simplified statement of the theorem known by this name.)\n"
msgstr ""
"A última implicação da equivalência unitária de purificações que discutiremos nesta parte da lição é o seguinte teorema, conhecido como o teorema de Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters.\n"
"(Esta é, de fato, uma versão ligeiramente simplificada do teorema conhecido por esse nome.)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters: Let $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ be systems and let $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ be a quantum state vector of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"Also let $N$ be an arbitrary positive integer, let $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{N-1})$ be a probability vector, and let $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ be quantum state vectors representing states of $\\mathsf{X}$ such that\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert\\bigr) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"There exists a (general) measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ on $\\mathsf{Y}$ such that the following two statements are true when this measurement is performed on $\\mathsf{Y}$ when $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is in the state $\\vert\\phi\\rangle:$\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Teorema\">\n"
"Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters: Sejam $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ sistemas e seja $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ um vetor de estado quântico do par $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"Seja também $N$ um inteiro positivo arbitrário, seja $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{N-1})$ um vetor de probabilidade, e sejam $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ vetores de estado quântico representando estados de $\\mathsf{X}$ tais que\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert\\bigr) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"Existe uma medição (geral) $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ em $\\mathsf{Y}$ tal que as duas afirmações a seguir são verdadeiras quando essa medição é realizada em $\\mathsf{Y}$ quando $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ está no estado $\\vert\\phi\\rangle:$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each measurement outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$ appears with probability $p_a$.\n"
msgstr "Cada resultado de medição $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$ aparece com probabilidade $p_a$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2. Conditioned on obtaining the measurement outcome $a$, the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle$.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"2. Condicionado à obtenção do resultado de medição $a$, o estado de $\\mathsf{X}$ passa a ser $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle$.\n"
"</Figure>\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, this theorem says that as long as we have a pure state of two systems, then for *any* way of thinking about the reduced state of the first system as a convex combination of pure states, there is a measurement of the second system that effectively makes this way of thinking about the first system a reality.\n"
"Notice that the number $N$ is not necessarily bounded by the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ or $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"For instance, it could be that $N = 1,000,000$ while $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Falando intuitivamente, esse teorema diz que desde que tenhamos um estado puro de dois sistemas, então para *qualquer* maneira de pensar sobre o estado reduzido do primeiro sistema como uma combinação convexa de estados puros, existe uma medição do segundo sistema que efetivamente torna essa maneira de pensar sobre o primeiro sistema uma realidade.\n"
"Note que o número $N$ não é necessariamente limitado pelo número de estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{X}$ ou $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Por exemplo, poderia ser que $N = 1.000.000$ enquanto $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ são qubits.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We shall prove this theorem using the unitary equivalence of purifications, beginning with the introduction of a new system $\\mathsf{Z}$ whose classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"Consider the following two quantum state vectors of the triple $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Vamos provar esse teorema usando a equivalência unitária de purificações, começando com a introdução de um novo sistema $\\mathsf{Z}$ cujo conjunto de estados clássicos é $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$.\n"
"Considere os dois vetores de estado quântico a seguir do triplo $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle & = \\vert\\phi\\rangle_{\\mathsf{XY}}\\otimes\\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle & = \\vert\\phi\\rangle_{\\mathsf{XY}}\\otimes\\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first vector $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ is simply the given quantum state vector $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ tensored with $\\vert 0\\rangle$ for the new system $\\mathsf{Z}$.\n"
"For the second vector $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle$, we essentially have a quantum state vector that would make the theorem trivial — at least if $\\mathsf{Y}$ were replaced by $\\mathsf{Z}$ — because a standard basis measurement performed on $\\mathsf{Z}$ clearly yields each outcome $a$ with probability $p_a$, and conditioned on obtaining this outcome the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"O primeiro vetor $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ é simplesmente o vetor de estado quântico dado $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ tensoriado com $\\vert 0\\rangle$ para o novo sistema $\\mathsf{Z}$.\n"
"Para o segundo vetor $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle$, essencialmente temos um vetor de estado quântico que tornaria o teorema trivial — pelo menos se $\\mathsf{Y}$ fosse substituído por $\\mathsf{Z}$ — porque uma medição na base padrão realizada em $\\mathsf{Z}$ claramente produz cada resultado $a$ com probabilidade $p_a$, e condicionado à obtenção desse resultado o estado de $\\mathsf{X}$ passa a ser $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By thinking about the pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ as a single, compound system that can be traced out to leave $\\mathsf{X}$, we find that we have identified two different purifications of the state\n"
msgstr "Ao pensar no par $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ como um único sistema composto que pode ser traçado para deixar $\\mathsf{X}$, encontramos que identificamos duas purificações diferentes do estado\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specifically, for the first one we have\n"
msgstr "Especificamente, para a primeira temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_0\\vert)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert) = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_0\\vert)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert) = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and for the second one we have\n"
msgstr "e para a segunda temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_1\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\rho.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_1\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\rho.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There must therefore exist a unitary operation $U$ on $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ satisfying\n"
msgstr "Deve, portanto, existir uma operação unitária $U$ em $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ satisfazendo\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert \\gamma_0 \\rangle = \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert \\gamma_0 \\rangle = \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "by the unitary equivalence of purifications.\n"
msgstr "pela equivalência unitária de purificações.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using this unitary operation $U$, we can implement a measurement that satisfies the requirements of the theorem as the following diagram illustrates.\n"
"In words, we introduce the new system $\\mathsf{Z}$ initialized to the $\\vert 0\\rangle$ state, apply $U$ to $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$, which transforms the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ from $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ into $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle$, and then measure $\\mathsf{Z}$ with a standard basis measurement, which we've already observed gives the desired behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"Usando essa operação unitária $U$, podemos implementar uma medição que satisfaz os requisitos do teorema como ilustra o diagrama a seguir.\n"
"Em palavras, introduzimos o novo sistema $\\mathsf{Z}$ inicializado no estado $\\vert 0\\rangle$, aplicamos $U$ a $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$, o que transforma o estado de $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ de $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ para $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle$, e então medimos $\\mathsf{Z}$ com uma medição na base padrão, que já observamos fornecer o comportamento desejado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit implementation of a measurement for the HSW theorem](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/purifications-and-fidelity/HSW-measurement.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Um circuito quântico implementando uma medição para o teorema HSW](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/purifications-and-fidelity/HSW-measurement.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The dotted rectangle in the figure represents an implementation of this measurement, which can be described as a collection of positive semidefinite matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ as follows.\n"
msgstr "O retângulo pontilhado na figura representa uma implementação dessa medição, que pode ser descrita como uma coleção de matrizes semidefinidas positivas $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ da seguinte forma.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert)U (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert)U (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
